==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/spɪl ðə biːnz/}}
* {{audio|en|En-au-spill the beans.ogg|Audio (AU)}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb|*|past2=spilt the beans}}

# {{lb|en|intransitive|idiomatic}} To [[reveal]] a [[secret]]; to [[disclose]].
#: {{ux|en|They had planned it as a surprise party, but somebody '''spilled the beans'''.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|April 5 2022|Tina Brown|How Princess Diana’s Dance With the Media Impacted William and Harry|Vanity Fair|url=https://www.vanityfair.com/style/2022/04/how-dianas-dance-with-the-media-impacted-william-and-harry?itm_content=footer-recirc&itm_campaign=more-great-stories-041222|footer=adapted from the book ''The Palace Papers'', published 2022 by Penguin Books|text=More unsettling was the origin story of the infamous tell-all book {{w|Princess in Love}}. {{w|Princess Diana|Diana}} claimed to be outraged in 1994 when {{w|Daily Express}} journalist Anna Pasternak '''spilled the beans''' of her affair with former army officer {{w|James Hewitt}}{{...}}}}

